  "wall.faces": "Walls are 3 rows: cap, upper face (wall.face.hi.*), lower face (wall.face.*). A wall-hung sprite (32px tall) fits the two face rows exactly.",
  "chalkboard": "Hang on the two face rows: object x = left px, y = wall base bottom edge (bottom-left of the sprite). The sprite already includes a 4px crown gap and 6px wainscot gap. 3 tiles wide; centre it on the room.",
  "chalkboard.tile": "No tile version: use the chalkboard sprite. For a DOM quiz card, anchor it to the sprite rect (x, y-32, 48, 32).",
  "foot": "foot.w = foot.h = 0 means non-blocking (wall-hung or floor decor)."
 }
